I've explored enough. Let me decide whether ask_questions is needed. The request: "add a strong password indicator when the user is trying to create a new account." Reasonably clear. Open questions: apply to all four signup surfaces or just main? Enforce minimum strength (block submit) or just show? I could make a sensible choice: show indicator everywhere, don't block (backend already validates length on some). Blocking could be a design decision though. I'll ask one quick question — actually the guidance says ask only for consequential decisions. Enforcing password strength on submit changes behavior (could block users). I'll ask that briefly. Or just make the sensible choice: indicator only, no blocking, mention in plan. That's arguably the sensible default — "indicator" implies display, not enforcement.

