## What now happens

The moment a scholarship is saved — from the provider panel, the admin panel, or the legacy `POST /api/scholarships` route — every active student account gets a formatted email and an in-app notification, dispatched in the background.

**Email content** ([emailService.js](Backend/services/emailService.js#L304)):
- **Subject:** `New Scholarship Opportunity: <name>` exactly as specified
- Scholarship title, provider name, award amount, deadline, and a short description excerpt
- A **Key Criteria** block with **Target GWA** (`GWA of 2.25 or better`), **Financial Need** (`rating of at least 4/5`, need-based programs, or priority sectors), **Education Level**, plus up to three specific criteria bullets
- CTA button → `/dashboard/scholarships?open=<id>`, which auto-opens that scholarship's detail dialog, plus a secondary "See scholarships matched to you" link
- All provider-supplied text is HTML-escaped, so a malicious scholarship name can't inject markup

**Delivery** ([newScholarshipNotificationService.js](Backend/services/newScholarshipNotificationService.js)):
- Recipients: all active student accounts (student + legacy customer roles, locked accounts skipped, emails deduped), salutation prefers `fullName`
- Runs via `setImmediate`, batches of 8 with a 400 ms pause so Gmail's SMTP isn't rate-limited
- **One blast per scholarship**: an atomic `notifiedAt` claim means a duplicate trigger or retry cannot email everyone twice
- Per-recipient failure isolation; in-app notification still created if email fails; if *every* send fails the claim is released so a retry can work
- Summary log: `"<name>" dispatched — sent: N, failed: N, recipients: N, in Xms`

**Hooks:** [provider.controller.js:168](Backend/controller/provider.controller.js#L168), [index.js:769](Backend/index.js#L769), [index.js:849](Backend/index.js#L849). The duplicate inline notifier in `index.js` was deleted; the model now declares `notifiedAt`/`notifiedCount` ([scholarship.model.js:28](Backend/models/scholarship.model.js#L28)).

## Verified

- **Real provider E2E** on an isolated `thesis_software_notification_test` DB: `POST /api/provider/scholarships` returned **201 in 0.95 s**, while the email took **3.2 s in the background** → `sent: 1, failed: 0`. `notifiedAt`/`notifiedCount` set, in-app notification row created.
- **One test email actually landed** in `gabrielcarpio12343@gmail.com` — subject `New Scholarship Opportunity: Notify Test Scholarship 2026` — so you can inspect the real rendering.
- **Duplicate trigger** → `recipients: 0`, no second email, notification count stayed 1.
- **Admin + legacy routes** → both 201 and both hit the notifier (verified with `Draft` scholarships, which correctly skip sending; total emails stayed at 1).
- **SMTP failure path** with wrong credentials → `sent: 0, failed: 1`, claim released, in-app notification still created, no crash.
- **Template assertions** passed: exact subject, GWA/financial-need/education criteria, `?open=<id>` CTA, escaping, no-id fallback.
- All five edited files pass `node --check`; the server boots clean.
- **Your real DB was not touched**: still 44 students, zero test scholarships/notifications in `thesis_software`. The scratch DB was dropped and the test server killed.

## Notes and limitations

- I changed `FRONTEND_BASE_URL` in [Backend/.env](Backend/.env) from a dead quick-tunnel host to `http://localhost:5173` — otherwise every CTA in the emails would have been unreachable. Set it to your public URL when demoing remotely.
- Dispatch is in-process: a server restart mid-blast drops the remaining recipients (the claim prevents a resend, not a resume). There's no durable queue.
- Gmail SMTP caps recipients per day; batching helps but a burst of many new scholarships could hit it.
- Signed-out recipients land on `/auth/signin` and lose the `?open=` parameter, because the dashboard guard has no post-login return path.
- I did not run the existing Jest suite — no test references the changed email function, and the DB-backed suites need their own environment.
